  "query_preview": "..\n\nRest of Today through Tuesday...\n\nUpper level ridging will dominate the forecast into the weekend, \nbringing above normal temperatures and dry conditions. High \ntemperatures are forecast to be in the 50s and 60sF each day. \nThursday looks to be the warmest day, with temperatures climbing \ntowards 70F for portions of southern Montana and northern Wyoming \nThursday.\n\nBreezy winds will linger across the foothills west of Billings\ninto this afternoon, with gusts in the 20s and 30s mph. A surface\nhigh will develop over the northern Midwest on Friday, bringing\nwindy conditions to eastern Montana with a tightening pressure\ngradient. Southerly winds gusting in the 30s to 40s mph are\ncurrently forecast, greatest across Carter and Fallon Counties. \nThese conditions look to continue through Saturday before the high\npressure moves east.\n\nEnsembles continue to show a wave moving through the region late\nSaturday or Sunday. The chance for precipitation is low across the\narea, outside of the southwest mountains where a few showers are \npossible. Otherwise, ensembles do not depict another chance for\nprecipitation until next Tuesday or Wednesday when an upper \ntrough could impact the region. For now, uncertainty remains high\nfor next week so continue to monitor the forecast.\n\nMatos",
